        "protocol_summary": "Current Finance (formerly Pebble Protocol) is a Sui DeFi lending protocol offering leveraged yield (up to 16x) via 1-click Multiply strategies on LSTs and yield-bearing assets, alongside on-chain isolated Margin markets. The protocol is based on Compound-style exchange rate, ctoken, and borrow index mechanics. It uses Pyth oracle for price feeds. Target chain: Sui. Language: Sui Move (edition 2024.beta). No public documentation site was found for Current Finance itself (current.fi returned 403, docs.current.fi unreachable).",
        "key_invariants_from_readme": [
          "Users cannot switch emode once obligations are created",
          "Only assets from the emode can be borrowed by an obligation",
          "Above invariants must hold under flash loan with reentrancy (flashloan + deposit/borrow in one PTB)",
          "Lending protocol is based on exchange rate, ctoken and borrow index",
          "Flashloan fees are tied to emode",
          "Liquidation bots may not liquidate on time - bad debt is possible",
          "Admin caps will be transferred to governance contract",
          "Only whitelisted tokens (LST), standard Sui Coin type supported"
        ],
